      "projectName": "Kukumuty",
      "projectDescription": "The Kukumuty project enhances the floristic biodiversity of Miombo woodlands within a broader agroecosystem mosaic to fight hunger by building up local food systems. Kukumuty works to enrich Miombo forests in and around Chibabava, Mozambique, entailing 300 ha in Nhaumue and 69 ha in Mangunde. The project also establishes agroforestry nurseries and plots for growing horticultural and fuelwood species. Core community benefits include the combination of fruit, nut, medicinal, and other useful native trees with the sustainable collection of grasses, honey and indigenous Miombo fruits.",
